<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew rises in technical bounce.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew rises in technical bounce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew Plc rose 3-3/4 pence to 177p in a technical bounce, after a prolonged period of underperfomance.</p>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew has underperformed the FTSE All Share Index by nearly 10 percent in the last four months.</p>
<p>Dealers said the company was recouping ground after the acquisition of fellow artificial limb maker De Puy Inc by Roche Holding AG.</p>
<p>The deal, announced on Monday, put the spotlight on Smith &amp; Nephew again, a trader said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
